.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

#ifdef __CYGWIN__
int server_winpipe_token_path(const char *name, char *buf, size_t bufsize);
#endif
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolves the filesystem path for the authentication token file used in
Named Pipe transport mode.
The token file stores the randomly generated authentication token that
clients must present to authenticate.
.PP
\f[B]Path resolution order:\f[R]
.IP "1." 3
If \f[CR]$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\f[R] is set and non\-empty:
.RS 4
.IP
.EX
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bash\-server/<name>.token
.EE
.RE
.IP "2." 3
Otherwise (fallback):
.RS 4
.IP
.EX
/tmp/bash\-server\-<uid>/<name>.token
.EE
.PP
Where \f[CR]<uid>\f[R] is the numeric UID from \f[CR]getuid()\f[R].
.RE
.PP
The parent directory (\f[CR]bash\-server/\f[R] or
\f[CR]bash\-server\-<uid>/\f[R]) is created with mode \f[CR]0700\f[R] if
it does not already exist.
The function handles \f[CR]EEXIST\f[R] gracefully (directory already
exists).
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]name\f[R] \(em Pipe name (same name passed to
\f[CR]server_winpipe_create()\f[R]).
Used as the token filename stem.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]buf\f[R] \(em Output buffer for the resolved path string.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]bufsize\f[R] \(em Size of the output buffer in bytes.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success (path written to \f[B]buf\f[R]).
.PP
Returns \-1 on error: \- Directory creation failed (neither exists nor
can be created).
Error details are printed to stderr.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]server_winpipe_create\f[R](3), \f[CR]server_winpipe_accept\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Cygwin only\f[R]: Compiled only when \f[CR]__CYGWIN__\f[R] is
defined.
.IP \(bu 2
The token file itself is not created by this function; it only resolves
the path.
The server main loop writes the token to this path after generating it.
.IP \(bu 2
The fallback path uses \f[CR]/tmp/\f[R], which on Cygwin maps to the
Windows temp directory.
The \f[CR]0700\f[R] permissions ensure only the owning user can access
the token.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]PATH_MAX\f[R] is used internally for the directory path buffer.
